      "content": "It's tempting to downplay the nausea data by highlighting that it was statistically insignificant or a minor outlier, but be cautious when doing so. If regulatory agencies or the FDA require more evidence, downplaying safety concerns can lead to a larger issue. Consider refreshing your regulatory submission and study reports to include the full and complete data on gastrointestinal tolerance, and then provide context on the minor reports. This might allow you to maintain the \"Maximum Comfort\" messaging while still meeting regulatory requirements.",
